.TH CHARCOAL 1 2026-11-19 "charcoal 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
charcoal \- terminal ASCII art viewer for images, animations and video
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B charcoal
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B charcoal
.I file
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B charcoal
.I folder
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B charcoal render
.I file
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B charcoal export
.I file
.B \-o
.I out
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B charcoal
shows images, animated images and video as character art in the terminal,
in a full-screen viewer with panels, live controls and playback.
Anything FFmpeg can decode opens: PNG, JPEG, WebP, AVIF, TIFF, GIF, APNG,
MP4, MKV, WebM and more.
Photos are turned upright from their EXIF orientation.
.PP
Without a file,
.B charcoal
opens the file picker on the current folder.
With a folder, it opens the folder's first image or video with the picker on
top.
.B render
prints one frame to standard output and exits;
.B export
writes it to a
.IR .txt ,
.I .ans
or
.I .html
file.
When standard output is not a terminal,
.B charcoal
.I file
behaves like
.BR render .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mode " " \fIMODE\fR
Glyph mode:
.B half
(two pixels per cell, the default),
.BR ascii ,
.B quad
(four pixels per cell),
.B braille
(eight dots per cell) or
.B edges
(lines along edges over ascii).
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-palette " " \fINAME\fR
Characters for
.B ascii
and
.BR edges ,
densest first:
.BR standard ,
.B detailed
(70 levels),
.BR simple ,
.BR blocks ,
or any string of your own.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-color " " \fIDEPTH\fR
.B auto
(the default),
.B true
(24-bit),
.BR 256 ,
.B 16
or
.BR mono .
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dither " " \fIKIND\fR
.B none
(the default),
.B floyd
(Floyd-Steinberg error diffusion) or
.B bayer
(an ordered pattern that stays steady in video).
.TP
.BI \-\-fit " KIND"
How the viewer fills its panel:
.B contain
(the default),
.B cover
or
.BR stretch .
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " NAME"
.BR gruvbox_dark ,
.BR nord ,
.BR tokyo_night ,
.BR mono ,
.BR tty ,
or a theme file (see
.BR THEMES ).
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-width " " \fIN\fR
Output width in characters
.RB ( render
and
.BR export ).
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-height " " \fIN\fR
Output height in characters
.RB ( render
and
.BR export ).
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-invert
Flip brightness.
charcoal assumes a dark terminal; use this on a light one.
.TP
.BI \-\-brightness " N"
\-1 to 1, 0 by default.
.TP
.BI \-\-contrast " N"
0 to 4, 1 by default.
.TP
.BI \-\-gamma " N"
0.1 to 5, 1 by default; higher brightens midtones.
.TP
.BI \-\-saturation " N"
0 to 4, 1 by default; 0 is grayscale.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-time " " \fISECONDS\fR
The frame shown at this time
.RB ( render
and
.BR export ).
.TP
.BI \-\-frame " N"
The
.IR N th
frame, counting from 0; wins over
.BR \-\-time .
Past the end gives the last frame.
.TP
.BR \-\-loop ", " \-\-no\-loop
Loop animations and video in the viewer (the default) or not.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIFILE\fR
Where
.B export
writes;
.IR .txt ,
.I .ans
or
.IR .html .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the usage.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and the FFmpeg and libwebp versions built in.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.BR "Up" ", " "Down" " (" j ", " k )
Pick a control.
.TP
.BR "Left" ", " "Right" " (" h ", " l )
Change the picked control.
.TP
.BR m " " M ", " p " " P ", " c " " C ", " d ", " i ", " f
Glyph mode, palette, color depth (next / previous), dither, invert, fit.
.TP
.BR b " " B ", " t " " T ", " g " " G ", " s " " S
Brightness, contrast, gamma and saturation up / down.
.TP
.BR + " " \-
Zoom in and out.
.TP
.BR Shift +arrows " (" H " " J " " K " " L )
Pan when zoomed in.
.TP
.B r
Reset zoom, pan and adjustments.
.TP
.BR n " " N
Next / previous image or video in the folder.
.TP
.B O
File picker: type to filter, Enter opens, Left or Backspace goes up.
.TP
.BR Space ", " , " " . ", " [ " " ] ", " { " " }
Play / pause, step a frame, seek 5 or 30 seconds.
.TP
.BR < " " > ", " R ", " Home
Playback speed, repeat, back to the start.
.TP
.BR 1 " to " 5
Show or hide the viewer, info, controls, histogram and timeline panels.
.TP
.B e
Export the view to
.IR .html ,
.I .ans
or
.IR .txt :
Tab switches between the folder and the file name,
.B Ctrl+O
browses for the folder,
.B Ctrl+U
clears a field.
The folder last exported to is remembered.
.TP
.BR o ", " F2
Options, saved to the config file.
.TP
.BR ? ", " F1
Every key.
.TP
.B Esc
The menu (options, help, quit); it closes whatever is open first.
.TP
.BR q ", " Ctrl+C
Quit.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Z
Suspend to the shell;
.B fg
comes back.
.TP
.B Ctrl+R
Reload the config file and theme.
.PP
The mouse works too: the wheel zooms toward the cursor or changes the
control under it, dragging pans or scrubs the timeline, and buttons, tabs
and lists are clickable.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/charcoal/charcoal.conf
Settings, written by the options overlay: lines of
.IB key " = " value
for
.BR theme ,
.BR theme_background ,
.BR rounded ,
.BR vim_keys ,
.BR mouse ,
.BR panels ,
.BR export_dir ,
.BR mode ,
.BR palette ,
.BR fit ,
.BR invert ,
.BR color ,
.BR dither ,
.BR brightness ,
.BR contrast ,
.BR gamma ,
.BR saturation ,
.B loop
and
.BR max_fps .
Command-line options override it.
.TP
.I ~/.config/charcoal/themes/NAME.theme
A theme.
.SH THEMES
A theme file holds lines like
.B main_bg = """#282828"""
for the keys
.BR main_bg ,
.BR main_fg ,
.BR title ,
.BR hi_fg ,
.BR selected_bg ,
.BR selected_fg ,
.BR inactive_fg ,
.BR box_border ,
.BR graph_low ,
.B graph_mid
and
.BR graph_high .
A color can also be
.B default
(the terminal's own) or a palette number from 0 to 255.
Missing keys keep the default theme's colors.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B COLORTERM
.B truecolor
or
.B 24bit
selects 24-bit color when the color depth is
.BR auto .
.TP
.B TERM
A name containing
.B 256color
selects 256 colors otherwise.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set, the automatic color depth is
.BR mono .
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Where the
.I charcoal
config folder lives, instead of
.IR ~/.config .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when a file cannot be opened or an option is wrong.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
charcoal
charcoal ~/Pictures
charcoal clip.mp4 \-\-theme nord
charcoal render photo.jpg \-m braille \-d floyd
charcoal render clip.mp4 \-t 12.5 \-w 100
charcoal export photo.jpg \-o photo.html
.fi
